r-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-24650" :question/id #uuid "1938b105-5884-5db6-9c07-161191c66b44" :question/math-academy-id "q-24650" :question/problem "$8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{5})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}) & =4\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{5})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{5})} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-24650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-24650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-24792/selection/6fb38bd9af42f00e1fe290593de532585d15dce8fde79a4010a278a346dcfa10" :answer/id #uuid "b1b24666-1aca-5be9-819d-d91bfb268761" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-24792/selection/830e992b15d86e65ebc14f66bc02db25c583f1c078a956092beea77c4ca08966" :answer/id #uuid "2a9b41f1-3aa5-5cc6-ab51-cbf27da442df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/