)\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡{210}^{∘} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n8\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120032/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
